---
layout: layouts/product.njk
title: "VoiceTel Phone — Desktop clients"
description: "VoiceTel Phone desktop clients for Windows, macOS, and Linux. Native SIP-over-TLS calling with system audio, call recording, and diagnostics."
---
{%- from "partials/v2/macros.njk" import arrow %}
{%- set voicetel = phoneApps.apps | where("key", "voicetel") | first %}
{%- set macDmg = voicetel.desktop | where("platform", "macos") | where("format", ".dmg") | where("arch", "arm64") | first %}
{%- set winSetup = voicetel.desktop | where("platform", "windows") | where("format", "Installer (.exe)") | first %}

<section class="hero hero--page" aria-labelledby="hero-heading">
	<div class="hero__bg" aria-hidden="true"></div>
	<div class="container hero__inner">
		<div class="hero__copy">
			<p class="eyebrow">VoiceTel Phone &middot; Desktop</p>
			<h1 id="hero-heading">Native desktop calling on Windows, macOS, and Linux.</h1>
			<p class="lede">A single VoiceTel identity across every desktop OS, with VoiceML Phone builds for VoiceML accounts on each install guide. SIP-over-TLS by default.</p>
			<div class="cta-row">
				<a class="btn btn--primary btn--lg" href="/signup/">Sign up {{ arrow(14) }}</a>
				<a class="btn btn--ghost btn--lg" href="/phone/applications/">All applications</a>
			</div>
		</div>
		<div class="hero__visual">
			{%- set platforms = [
				{ icon: "hdd-stack", name: "Windows", meta: winSetup.size ~ " · .exe", href: "/phone/applications/desktop/windows/" },
				{ icon: "hdd-stack", name: "macOS", meta: macDmg.size ~ " · .dmg", href: "/phone/applications/desktop/macos/" },
				{ icon: "hdd-stack", name: "Linux", meta: "AppImage · deb · rpm", href: "/phone/applications/desktop/linux/" }
			] %}
			{% include "partials/v2/platform-grid.njk" %}
		</div>
	</div>
</section>

<section class="section section--tint" id="clients" aria-labelledby="clients-heading">
	<div class="container">
		<div class="section__head">
			<p class="eyebrow">Desktop clients</p>
			<h2 id="clients-heading">Native clients for Windows, macOS, and Linux.</h2>
			<p class="lede">System-audio integration, local call recording, and the diagnostics surface needed for support escalations, on every desktop OS.</p>
		</div>
		{%- set features = [
			{ icon: "layers", title: "Windows", body: "Native Windows client with system-audio routing, Windows notification integration, and a choice of setup installer (.exe), portable executable, or .zip archive. Tested across recent Windows 10 and 11 builds.", href: "/phone/applications/desktop/windows/", cta: "Windows install guide" },
			{ icon: "layers", title: "macOS", body: "Native macOS client signed and notarized for Gatekeeper. Drag-to-Applications .dmg installer or .zip for IT-managed deployment. Audio integrates with the macOS sound preferences and supports AirPods + USB DAC routing.", href: "/phone/applications/desktop/macos/", cta: "macOS install guide" },
			{ icon: "layers", title: "Linux", body: "Distro-agnostic AppImage for portable use, .deb and .rpm packages for Debian/Ubuntu and Fedora/RHEL, plus Snap and Flatpak, with arm64 builds for 64-bit ARM. Uses PulseAudio or PipeWire for sound routing depending on the system configuration.", href: "/phone/applications/desktop/linux/", cta: "Linux install guide" }
		] %}
		{% include "partials/v2/feature-grid.njk" %}
	</div>
</section>

<section class="section section--white" id="requirements" aria-labelledby="requirements-heading">
	<div class="container">
		<div class="row">
			<div class="row__text">
				<p class="eyebrow">What you'll need</p>
				<h2 id="requirements-heading">SIP credentials and a working microphone are all it takes.</h2>
				<p class="lede">VoiceTel SIP credentials are provisioned from the customer portal after signup; VoiceML Phone takes a VoiceML activation code instead. Add a working microphone and audio output device.</p>
			</div>
			<div class="row__visual">
				{%- set rows = [
					{ title: "VoiceTel SIP credentials", meta: "provisioned from the customer portal after signup", state: "Required" },
					{ title: "VoiceML activation code", meta: "for VoiceML Phone, in place of SIP credentials", state: "VoiceML Phone", neutral: true },
					{ title: "Microphone and audio output", meta: "a working input and output device", state: "Required" }
				] %}
				{% include "partials/v2/status-card.njk" %}
			</div>
		</div>

		<div class="cta-band">
			<div class="cta-band__text">
				<h3 class="cta-band__title">Need credentials first?</h3>
				<p class="cta-band__body">Sign up to provision SIP credentials, then install the desktop client on every workstation that needs it.</p>
			</div>
			<div class="cta-band__actions cta-row">
				<a class="btn btn--primary" href="/signup/">Free trial {{ arrow(14) }}</a>
				<a class="btn btn--ghost" href="/phone/applications/">All applications</a>
			</div>
		</div>
	</div>
</section>
